// Renovate — the update lane for `mise.toml [tools]`, the one dependency surface
// no other bot can read (CLOUD-655).
//
// JSON5 rather than JSON so the reasoning lives beside the keys it explains. The
// keys here are not preferences: four of them are the whole CI-cost mechanism,
// and `mise run ci-local-parity` refuses this file if any of the four is dropped.
//
// WHY A SECOND BOT AT ALL. Dependabot's `package-ecosystem` values are a fixed
// published list with no `mise`, no asdf `.tool-versions` and no
// `rust-toolchain`, so `.github/dependabot.yml` cannot cover this repo's tool
// table at any setting. That is a capability gap, not a config omission, and its
// cost was measured: `[tools] rust` sat at 1.85.0 against a stable of 1.97.1 —
// twelve releases — freezing two crates and rejecting a third, with `mise run
// lock-check` green throughout because it asks a different currency question
// (have the artifacts for the versions we ALREADY pinned changed).
//
// TWO BOTS OVER DISJOINT MANIFESTS IS NOT TWO AUTHORITIES FOR ONE FACT. Each
// manifest gets exactly one updater, and `ci-local-parity` decides that rather
// than trusting the comment: an ecosystem covered by both bots, or by neither,
// fails the gate.
//
// THIS LANE PROPOSES NOTHING UNTIL SOMEONE INSTALLS RENOVATE. The config is
// inert without the Renovate GitHub App on the `button-inc` org (or Renovate
// self-hosted as a scheduled Actions run with a token that can open PRs). That
// is an owner action and deliberately not a code change; the config and its gate
// land regardless, so the day the app arrives there is nothing left to write.
{
  $schema: "https://docs.renovatebot.com/renovate-schema.json",

  extends: ["config:recommended"],

  // THE SCOPE FENCE, and it is load-bearing rather than tidy. `config:recommended`
  // enables every manager Renovate ships with, which would silently make this a
  // SECOND updater for `cargo` and for the workflows — both of which Dependabot
  // owns at this commit. `enabledManagers` is an allowlist, so naming `mise`
  // alone is what keeps the disjointness above true by construction.
  // CLOUD-657 and CLOUD-658 add the other two here, each in the same commit that
  // removes them from `.github/dependabot.yml`.
  enabledManagers: ["mise"],

  // --- the four keys `ci-local-parity` holds ---------------------------------
  //
  // Every `pull_request` workflow in this repo gates on `draft == false`, so a
  // draft head buys zero runner minutes. Dependabot's schema has no equivalent
  // knob, which is why its lane was measured at 13 `ci.yml` runs and zero skips
  // over eight days (CLOUD-596) — a full matrix per SHA it proposes. CLOUD-596
  // priced the workaround (a new workflow and a PAT-driven ready) and declined
  // it. This is one key.
  draftPR: true,

  // The default force-pushes a rebase whenever the base moves, and on a readied
  // PR each force-push is a `synchronize` and another matrix. `main` advances
  // constantly here, so that default is a matrix per landing by anyone.
  rebaseWhen: "never",

  // With rebasing off, a stale PR can be joined by a sibling proposing the same
  // update — doubling the floor the key above lowers. Both keys or neither
  // works, which is the same pairing `.github/dependabot.yml` carries.
  prConcurrentLimit: 1,

  // Renovate's spelling of the 7-day cooldown CLOUD-105 bought on the Dependabot
  // lanes: let a churny release settle before a PR opens.
  minimumReleaseAge: "7 days",

  // --- and the key without which none of the above can ever land -------------
  //
  // Every commit here must satisfy `CONVENTIONAL_RE` (the `commit-lint` gate),
  // because PRs land by fast-forward. Renovate's default subject carries no type
  // prefix, so its PRs would fail commit-lint and could never land — the same
  // defect `.github/dependabot.yml`'s `commit-message.prefix` settings exist to
  // avoid. `ci` rather than `build`: this table pins the toolchain CI and the
  // hooks run, not the crate's dependency graph.
  semanticCommits: "enabled",
  semanticCommitType: "ci",
  semanticCommitScope: "deps",
}
